arges  against Weinstein for that  case in particular but the prosecution  was hoping that her story along with  three other women who also testified  that they were raped or assaulted by him  would give them enough evidence to  convict on this higher charge which  carried up to life in prison for  Weinstein now he's still likely to do  some time and he's not clear of charges  either there's also charges pending in  Los Angeles against him as a result but  so not the full verdict that prosecutors  were hoping for but certainly some time  behind bars is now likely for for this  famous Hollywood producer and also  Kristen interestingly Weinstein was  found not guilty of first-degree rape  but guilty of third-degree rape which I  thought was an interesting outcome tell  us about the complainants in this case I  believe there were two women whose  accounts were being considered in the  trial yes the two guilty charges relate  to a an aspiring actress and a  production assistant who they say were  forced into these relationships as you  know this case against Harvey Weinstein  really prompted a national movement  known as the me2 movement there were  countless women who came forward after  reports began surfacing in the media  there had been rumors about Harvey  Weinstein being this lecherous producer  for years it was kind of circulating a  lot of media outlets did not want to  touch the story because he was just so  powerful but when some women came  forward including the actress Rose  McGowan and started talking about it on  social media it prompted women around  the country to talk about their own  cases of sexual abuse we saw people  coming out in droves outside of the  courthouse when Harvey Weinstein showed  up women's groups chanting and taunting  him because of this movement that he  inspired it really helped expose some of  the the dirty secrets of Hollywood in  many industries where men of power had  taken advance  of women and it caused so many women to  speak out that this case really  resonated and continues to resonate for  women around the country and around the  globe but again he will not face the  most severe charges the most severe  charges the jury found that there wasn't  enough evidence to convict him but a  partial victory for women who were  looking for some justice for Harvey  Weinstein my colleague Gabe Elizondo  actually has more about the history of  Weinstein's case and the movement that  he inspired Harvey Weinstein was not  just any movie producer  but maybe one of the most powerful ever  many of the greatest actors or actresses  over the past 40 years have worked with  him in some capacity either directly or  through his movie studios throughout his  career Weinstein has 81 Academy Awards  to his name and his power extended into  politics at the very highest of levels  from Bill and Hillary Clinton who called  him a personal friend to Barack and  Michelle Obama one of their daughters  briefly worked for Weinstein to Donald  Trump who often was at the same New York  events but it was Weinstein's influence  in Hollywood and his ability to make or  break an actor's career where he had his  most power and according to prosecutors  he wielded that power by sexually  exploiting women  he's been on trial in New York for  allegedly raping an aspiring actress in  2013 and sexually assaulting another  woman in 2006 for other women testified  against him saying they too were victims  more than a hundred other women many  anonymously have come out publicly and  said they too were assaulted by  Weinstein during the four week trial  prosecutors told the 12-person jury  Weinstein was a serial rapist and  manipulator his defense argued otherwise  if you look at all the evidence the  evidence shows consensual relationship  in 2017 the New York Times first  reported allegations of abuse against  Weinstein sparking women to come forward  and talking about abuse at the hands of  more powerful men actress Alyssa Milano 